@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Get available units count (200) - will be cached
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01&endDate=2025-11-05

### Get available units count for different period (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-12-01&endDate=2025-12-10

### Get available units count - same period (200) - should return from cache
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01&endDate=2025-11-05

### Negative: Invalid date range - end before start (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-05&endDate=2025-11-01

### Negative: Equal dates (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01&endDate=2025-11-01

### Negative: Missing parameters (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01

### Cache invalidation test workflow:
### Step 1: Get count (will be cached)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01&endDate=2025-11-05

### Step 2: Create booking (will invalidate cache)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "unitId": 4,
  "userId": 4,
  "startDate": "2025-11-02",
  "endDate": "2025-11-04"
}

### Step 3: Get count again (cache miss, should recalculate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01&endDate=2025-11-05

### Step 4: Cancel booking (will invalidate cache)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/2/cancel

### Step 5: Get count again (cache miss, should recalculate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/statistics/available-units?startDate=2025-11-01&endDate=2025-11-05